# Turnback Cave (the original's D_03 role): the fog-filled cave beyond Sendoff Spring whose rooms are all alike and
# lead back to the entrance unless the way is kept, past three ancient pillars, down to the doorway of the Distortion
# World. Four rooms of one phrase: a low flute sighs over a pad, the vibraphone drips and echoes the phrase's tail,
# and each room is the last a minor third higher. The phrase keeps to one octatonic scale, which a minor third maps
# onto itself, so every room is made of the very same notes and the same diminished doorway chord closes each one.
# Then the pillars: a bell tolls three times, the bass falls by whole tones, a low clarinet chants over a choir, and a
# ii-V turns back into C minor at the entrance again. Original composition for this game.
title Turnback Cave
tempo 72
meter 4/4
reverb 0.55
night none

